  height: fit-content;
  background-color: inherit !important;
}

.dv-tabs-and-actions-container .dv-tabs-container > .dv-tab.dv-inactive-tab,
.dv-tab {
  background-color: inherit;
}

.dv-groupview.dv-active-group > .dv-tabs-and-actions-container .dv-tabs-container > .dv-tab.dv-inactive-tab,
.dv-groupview.dv-active-group > .dv-tabs-and-actions-container .dv-tabs-container > .dv-tab.dv-active-tab {
    background-color: inherit;
    color: inherit;
}
</style>
```

| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `client/src/components/desktop/Desktop.vue` | Modify | `onReady()` method | Moved `setDesktopApi()` call BEFORE `restoreLayout()` to ensure API is available; changed flow to set API then restore |

---

## Summary of Fixes

**Root Causes Identified**:
1. **Race Condition**: Views loaded before Desktop API was set → restoration failed silently
2. **Missing Fallback**: No default view creation for new projects → empty state persisted
3. **Storage Key Inconsistency**: Using `project_name` instead of `project_id` → could fail with name changes
4. **No Empty View Handling**: `onLayoutChanged()` expected `lastView` to always exist

**Solutions Applied**:
- Storage key now uses immutable `project_id` 
- Desktop API set BEFORE view restoration in `onReady()`
- Default empty view auto-created on first layout change
- `restoreProjectLayout()` creates view if none exists (new project scenario)
- Removed premature `autoLoadLastView()` call in `onActiveProjectChanged()`

